# Python bytecode and cache artefacts. The repository tracks source only;
# every session's working tree was accumulating untracked __pycache__/
# *.pyc directories (and three historically tracked .pyc blobs) that churn
# `git status` and pollute the executable-input fingerprint used by
# scripts/record_test_claim.py. These rules make that state explicit and
# reproducible rather than a per-session accident.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Distribution / packaging
*.egg-info/
*.egg
build/
dist/
.eggs/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Oversized generated F1GRID-002 artifacts.
# The two ledgers below are genuine grid outputs (~166 MB and ~69 MB) that
# exceed GitHub's hard 100 MB / recommended 50 MB file-size limits and block
# the pre-receive hook on push. They are generated, reproducible from the
# committed 216-cell grid summary, and must never be tracked. Prior sessions
# (14, 17, 18, 19, 20, 23) repeatedly re-added them in checkpoint commits,
# which is why the rule is declared here and guarded by
# tests/test_bytecode_hygiene.py rather than left to per-session discipline.
artifacts/HARMONY-CRYPTO-EDGE-004-DISPERSION-003-F1GRID-002/grid_result_ledger.json
artifacts/HARMONY-CRYPTO-EDGE-004-DISPERSION-003-F1GRID-002/grid_checkpoints/cell_checkpoint_armB_f1_repaired_ledger_vintage.json